title: 3. A plan is one note of a page or two, whose headlines are its decisions.
pid: 52f44494-0400-4a4b-9837-b791929bf77c
body: |2-
  Its first lines: its state (proposed, being built, built or
  abandoned), its signs and tier (step 4), the request, linked, and the
  appetite. Then goals and non-goals; the decisions, each stating
  itself, its body giving the alternatives rejected and whether it is
  a one-way door; questions for Jeff, each with a recommended answer
  and what is built if he does not answer; and the building missions,
  each with its objective, what it may touch, and its check. Where
  one part sends what another receives, the plan gives a whole example
  of it before either is built.
  Why, and its sources: [[id:276877af-a0fb-42ab-9e68-909b62c8d67b][step 3, its reasons]].
